    group: "Default & Termination",
    states: ["RI"],
    supersedes: "early-termination-ks",
    bodyText:
      "Tenant may terminate this Lease before the end of the Term by providing Landlord at least 30 days' written notice. Tenant will pay Landlord, by the termination date, an early termination fee equal to one month's Rent ({{monthly_rent}}), and remains responsible for Rent and other obligations up to the termination date. If Tenant gives that notice, pays the fee and delivers possession of the property by the termination date, Tenant owes no Rent for any period after the termination date. If Tenant leaves before the end of the Term without using this option, Tenant's liability is governed by Rhode Island law, including Landlord's duty to make reasonable efforts to re-rent the property. This fee is also listed with the Rent in the Rent section of this Lease. This early-termination option and fee apply only if this Lease has a fixed Term; a month-to-month or other periodic tenancy ends on the notice that Rhode Island law and this Lease provide, without an early termination fee. Landlord may end this Lease early only under this Lease's Tenant Default and notice provisions, any other section of this Lease that expressly lets Landlord end it, or, if Tenant abandons the property as Rhode Island law defines abandonment, after Landlord sends the certified-letter notice Rhode Island law requires, and Landlord will recover possession only as Rhode Island law allows. No early termination fee applies when Tenant ends this Lease under a right Rhode Island or federal law gives, including as a servicemember, as a tenant 65 or older entering assisted living, a nursing facility or elderly housing, as a survivor of abuse, domestic violence, sexual assault or stalking, after a fire or casualty, or because of Landlord's noncompliance. Nothing in this Section limits any right either party has under applicable law.",
