    bodyText:
      "COLLECTION COSTS. If Tenant fails to pay rent or any other amount owed under this Lease when due, Tenant will pay Landlord, in addition to the amount owed, (a) the actual, reasonable third-party collection costs Landlord incurs in collecting it, including the fee Landlord is obligated to pay a collection agency licensed under Wyo. Stat. § 33-11-102 to which Landlord refers the debt, and (b) Landlord's reasonable attorney's fees and court costs incurred in collecting it. Landlord will give Tenant written notice of the unpaid amount before referring the debt for collection.\n\nRETURNED PAYMENTS. If a check or electronic payment from Tenant is dishonored for any reason, Tenant will pay Landlord a returned-payment charge of [amount] plus any fee Landlord's bank charges Landlord. Landlord may also pursue the remedies in Wyo. Stat. § 1-1-115, which allow Landlord, after making the written demand that statute requires, to recover the amount of the check, a collection fee of thirty dollars ($30.00), and, if Tenant does not pay within thirty (30) days of that demand, three (3) times the amount of the check (not less than one hundred dollars ($100.00)) and court costs. Landlord will not recover twice for the same dishonored payment.\n\nATTORNEY'S FEES. In an action for possession based on Tenant's failure to pay rent, Landlord may recover the rent found due together with costs and attorney's fees as provided by this Lease, under Wyo. Stat. § 1-21-1008(b).",
