    bodyText:
      "Tenant will give Landlord written notice of the location where payment of any deposit balance and any notice about it may be made or mailed. Tenant will give that notice within thirty (30) days after this Agreement terminates, as required by Wyo. Stat. § 1-21-1208(a), and Tenant is encouraged to give it at or before move-out so the refund is not delayed. The notice must be in writing and must give a street or mailing address; Tenant may also give an email address, but an email address alone does not satisfy this paragraph. If Tenant does not give Landlord an address, Landlord will deliver or mail the deposit balance and the written itemization of deductions to the last address Landlord has for Tenant, which may be the property. Tenant will also give Landlord at least {{surrender_notice_days}} days' written notice before Tenant surrenders possession, and will tell Landlord the date Tenant will deliver the keys. Landlord will deliver or mail the balance of the deposit and prepaid rent, with a written itemization of any deductions and the reasons for them, within thirty (30) days after termination of this Agreement or within fifteen (15) days after Landlord receives Tenant's new mailing address, whichever is later, and that period is extended by thirty (30) days if there is damage to the property.",
