    bodyText:
      "Tenant, every other occupant, and any guest or other person under Tenant's control will not engage in, facilitate or permit any criminal activity on or near the Premises, and specifically will not manufacture, possess, use, sell, distribute, deliver or dispose of any controlled substance, or possess any drug paraphernalia, on or about the Premises, the building, the common areas or the grounds, except for a drug lawfully prescribed to an occupant and kept in its original container. Tenant will not maintain, use or permit the Premises to be used for lewdness, assignation, prostitution, gambling, or the manufacture, possession, sale or disposition of intoxicating liquor or any controlled substance in violation of law, each of which is a nuisance under Wyo. Stat. § 6-6-201 that places this property and its contents at risk of injunction, closure and sale. Tenant will not permit any person to bring onto or store at the Premises any equipment, glassware, solvent, precursor or other material used to manufacture a controlled substance.\n\nTenant will notify Landlord in writing within twenty-four hours of learning of any such activity at the Premises or in the building, and will cooperate fully with Landlord and with law enforcement in connection with it.\n\nEach obligation in this section is a material term of this Lease and of the rules and regulations imposed under it. A violation by Tenant, by any occupant, or by a guest or other person under Tenant's control is a material breach of this Lease, whether or not any person is arrested, charged or convicted, and whether or not the activity occurred in Tenant's presence or with Tenant's knowledge, and entitles Landlord to terminate this Lease and to pursue forcible entry and detainer and any other remedy available at law, after serving the notice to quit required by Wyo. Stat. § 1-21-1003. Proof in an eviction proceeding is by the civil standard and does not require a criminal conviction.\n\nIf a clandestine laboratory operation is found at the Premises, Tenant will be liable to Landlord for all resulting remediation, decontamination, response and holding costs that Landlord incurs or is assessed, to the full extent permitted by law.",
