    id: "eminent-domain-wy",
    title: "Condemnation and Eminent Domain",
    group: "Default & Termination",
    states: ["WY"],
    bodyText:
      "If all of the Premises are taken by eminent domain or conveyed under threat of condemnation, this Lease terminates and Tenant's obligation to pay rent ends on the earlier of the date the condemnor is permitted by court order to take possession or the date title transfers to the condemnor. If only part of the Premises is taken, this Lease continues as to the remainder and the rent is reduced, from that same date, in the proportion that the value of the part taken bears to the value of the whole Premises; but if the part taken is essential to Tenant's use of the Premises as a residence, or the remainder is no longer suitable as a residence, either Landlord or Tenant may terminate this Lease by written notice to the other given within thirty (30) days after the date of taking, and rent is prorated to the termination date. Landlord has no obligation to restore, rebuild or replace the Premises or to provide Tenant with substitute premises. Landlord is entitled to the award for the taking of Landlord's interest in the Premises. This paragraph does not affect or impair Tenant's right to compensation for the taking of Tenant's leasehold interest or Tenant's personal property, or Tenant's right to relocation assistance or a replacement housing payment from a displacing agency under Wyo. Stat. §§ 16-7-101 through 16-7-112. Landlord will give Tenant written notice of a condemnation proceeding affecting the Premises promptly after Landlord learns of it.",
