      "[Use only if the Premises include a parking space, garage or carport.] Electric Vehicle Charging. Tenant will not install, attach, or have installed any electric vehicle charging station, dedicated receptacle, outlet, wiring, conduit, subpanel or other charging equipment at the Premises without Landlord's prior written consent. Tenant will not charge an electric or plug-in hybrid vehicle from any outlet at the Premises except an outlet Landlord has designated in writing for that use, and will not run a cord across a walkway, driveway, stairway, common area or doorway.\n\nIf Landlord consents to an installation, Tenant will, before work begins: give Landlord the proposed equipment's make, model and electrical load and the proposed location; use an electrical contractor licensed in Wyoming and obtain every permit and inspection the city or county requires, giving Landlord a copy of each permit and final inspection approval; and give Landlord a certificate of insurance naming Landlord as an additional insured, covering Tenant's obligations under this Section, which Tenant will keep in force for as long as the equipment remains installed. Tenant will pay all costs of the installation, including any wiring, panel or service upgrade it requires, and all costs of maintaining and repairing the equipment.\n\nTenant is responsible for all damage arising from the equipment or its use, including damage from fire, overheating or electrical fault, and will indemnify Landlord against claims arising from it, except to the extent caused by Landlord. At the end of the tenancy the equipment will [remain in place and become Landlord's property / be removed by Tenant, who will restore the Premises to their prior condition and repair any damage]: [choose one]. Tenant will comply with Landlord's reasonable written rules on the dimensions, placement, appearance and hours of use of the equipment.\n\nElectricity for charging is [included in Rent and not separately charged / supplied under a flat charge of $______ per month, which is not a sale of electricity by the kilowatt hour]: [choose one]. Landlord does not meter or resell electricity to Tenant by the kilowatt hour, and Tenant will not resell, submeter or dispense electricity from the Premises to any other person.",
