      "Tenant will use the Premises only as a private residence. If Tenant will be away from the Premises for more than seven (7) consecutive days, Tenant will notify Landlord in writing no later than the first day of the absence, and will tell Landlord how Tenant can be reached and who, if anyone, Tenant has authorized to enter the Premises during the absence. Tenant remains responsible for the rent and for all of Tenant's other obligations under this Lease during any absence. If Tenant fails to give the notice this paragraph requires, Tenant is responsible to Landlord for the damages Landlord actually sustains as a result of not having it.\n\nTenant's absence alone does not end this Lease. Landlord may treat the Premises as abandoned, and this Lease as terminated under Wyo. Stat. § 1-21-1201(a)(v), only if all of the following are true: Tenant has been absent from the Premises for at least fifteen (15) consecutive days without giving Landlord the notice required above; rent is unpaid and at least seven (7) days overdue; and the circumstances reasonably indicate that Tenant has given up the Premises, such as removal of substantially all of Tenant's belongings, return of the keys, written notice from Tenant, or disconnection of utilities in Tenant's name. Before treating the Premises as abandoned, Landlord will make reasonable efforts to contact Tenant at the telephone number, e-mail address and emergency contact Tenant has given Landlord. Nothing in this paragraph authorizes Landlord to recover possession of the Premises other than as Wyoming law allows, and if Tenant disputes that the Premises were abandoned, Landlord will proceed under Wyo. Stat. §§ 1-21-1001 through 1-21-1017 rather than by self-help.",
