      "[Choose paragraph A or paragraph B. Do not leave this subject out of the lease: under Wyo. Stat. § 34-1-501 a covenant that does not clearly and expressly prohibit child care does not prohibit it, and day care for up to ten children is treated as a residential use.] A. Prohibited. Landlord and Tenant clearly and expressly agree that Tenant will not provide child care or day care at the property for any child other than a child who resides at the property, and will not operate, host or allow a child care home, family day care home, day care home, day care facility, preschool or nursery at the property, whether or not the activity requires certification under Wyo. Stat. §§ 14-4-101 through 14-4-115, and whether or not Tenant is paid. This paragraph is a clear and express prohibition of child care for the purposes of Wyo. Stat. § 34-1-501. B. Permitted on conditions. Tenant may provide child care at the property for not more than {{max_children_in_care}} children at any one time, on all of these conditions: (1) Tenant obtains and keeps in force every certification, license, registration and local permit the activity requires, including any certification required by Wyo. Stat. §§ 14-4-101 through 14-4-115, and gives Landlord a copy of each within ten (10) days of issuance and of any renewal, suspension or revocation; (2) Tenant carries liability insurance covering claims for injury to children in Tenant's care and to the children's parents and guests at the property, in an amount of not less than ${{child_care_liability_amount}}, names Landlord as an additional insured, and gives Landlord a certificate of insurance before care begins and at each renewal; (3) Tenant will not use any common area, shared hallway, shared stair, shared yard or parking area for the care activity except for passage to and from the property, and will not place signs, play equipment or fencing anywhere outside the property without Landlord's prior written consent; (4) Tenant is responsible for any damage to the property or to the building caused by the care activity, including damage caused by a child in Tenant's care or by that child's parent or guest; (5) Tenant will indemnify and hold Landlord harmless from any claim, loss, damage, cost or attorney's fee arising out of the care activity, to the extent not caused by Landlord's own negligence or by Landlord's failure to perform a duty Landlord owes under Wyo. Stat. §§ 1-21-1202 and 1-21-1203; and (6) Landlord may end Tenant's permission under this paragraph on thirty (30) days' written notice if Tenant breaches any condition of it, and Tenant will stop providing care at the property by the end of that period. Permission under this paragraph is permission to conduct the activity only, and does not change the number of occupants permitted at the property under this Agreement.",
