      "[Use only if Landlord gives Tenant a rent concession. Delete if none.] In consideration of Tenant entering into this Lease and performing it for its full Term, Landlord gives Tenant the following rent concession, which is part of this Lease and is not a separate agreement: {{concession_description}} -- a total value of ${{concession_total_value}}, applied as follows: {{concession_application}}. Rent for each month of the Term is ${{monthly_rent}}; the concession reduces what Tenant actually pays in the month or months described above and does not change the monthly Rent stated in this Lease for any other purpose, including the calculation of any amount Tenant owes on an early termination.\n\nIf before the end of the Term Tenant vacates the Premises without Landlord's written consent, Tenant gives notice of an early termination that this Lease does not permit, or Landlord lawfully terminates this Lease because of Tenant's breach, then the unearned portion of the concession becomes immediately due and payable to Landlord as an obligation under this Lease. The unearned portion is the total value of the concession multiplied by the number of whole months remaining in the Term on the date of the triggering event, divided by the total number of months in the Term. Tenant owes nothing under this paragraph if the Term runs to its end, if Tenant terminates under a right this Lease or Wyoming law gives Tenant, or if Tenant terminates under Wyo. Stat. §§ 1-21-1301 through 1-21-1304. Landlord may deduct the amount owed under this paragraph from the deposit only to the extent Wyo. Stat. § 1-21-1208 allows a deduction, and Landlord's right to recover it is not limited to the deposit.",
