    bodyText:
      "Tenant will pay each installment of Rent in full on the date it is due, without demand, and without any deduction, set-off, abatement or withholding, including on account of the condition of the property, a repair Tenant believes is needed, a repair Tenant has made or paid for, a utility interruption, or any claim Tenant has or believes Tenant has against Landlord. Wyoming law gives a renter no right to withhold rent, no right to repair and deduct, and no right to pay rent into escrow. If Tenant believes the property does not meet the health and safety standards of Wyo. Stat. §§ 1-21-1201 through 1-21-1211, Tenant's route is the one the statute gives: while remaining current on all payments required by this Agreement, Tenant must advise Landlord in writing of the condition and specify the remedial action Tenant requests, served by certified mail or in the manner specified by Wyo. Stat. § 1-21-1003, as Wyo. Stat. § 1-21-1203(b) provides. Landlord will then, within a reasonable time after receiving that notice, either begin action to correct the condition or notify Tenant in writing that Landlord disputes the claim. Tenant's payment of Rent in full does not waive any claim Tenant may bring under Wyo. Stat. § 1-21-1206, and nothing in this paragraph limits any right Tenant has under Wyo. Stat. §§ 1-21-1201 through 1-21-1211 or under the Wyoming Safe Homes Act, Wyo. Stat. §§ 1-21-1301 through 1-21-1304. Landlord's acceptance of a partial payment of Rent is not a waiver of the balance or of any default.",
