    bodyText:
      "NONREFUNDABLE DEPOSIT STATEMENT (Wyo. Stat. § 1-21-1207). This Lease states whether any portion of the deposit is nonrefundable, as Wyoming law requires. Landlord has selected one of the following, and the unselected alternative does not apply.\n\n[ ] ALTERNATIVE A - NO NONREFUNDABLE PORTION. No portion of any deposit paid by Tenant under this Lease is nonrefundable. The entire deposit of $__________ is refundable, subject to the deductions Wyo. Stat. § 1-21-1208(a) permits.\n\n[ ] ALTERNATIVE B - PART OF THE DEPOSIT IS NONREFUNDABLE. Of the total deposit of $__________ paid by Tenant under this Lease, the sum of $__________ is NONREFUNDABLE and will not be returned to Tenant at any time or for any reason. The nonrefundable portion is charged for: __________________________. The remaining $__________ is refundable, subject to the deductions Wyo. Stat. § 1-21-1208(a) permits.\n\nSEPARATE WRITTEN NOTICE. Wyo. Stat. § 1-21-1207 also requires Landlord to give Tenant written notice of the nonrefundable character of any deposit at the time the deposit is taken. Landlord gave Tenant that separate written notice on __________ (date), at the time the deposit was taken, and Tenant acknowledges receiving it. A copy is attached as an exhibit to this Lease.\n\nREFUNDABLE PORTION; ACCOUNTING. The refundable portion of the deposit, together with any prepaid rent, will be handled under Wyo. Stat. § 1-21-1208(a). Landlord may apply it to accrued rent, to damage to the unit beyond reasonable wear and tear, to the cost of cleaning the unit to the condition it was in at the beginning of this Lease, and to other costs provided by this Lease. Landlord will deliver or mail the balance, without interest, together with a written itemization of each deduction and the reason for it, within thirty (30) days after termination of this Lease or within fifteen (15) days after Landlord receives Tenant's new mailing address, whichever is later; if the unit is damaged, that period is extended by thirty (30) days.\n\nTENANT'S FORWARDING ADDRESS. Wyo. Stat. § 1-21-1208(a) requires Tenant, within thirty (30) days after termination of this Lease, to notify Landlord or Landlord's designated agent of the location where payment and notice may be made or mailed. Tenant should give that address in writing.\n\nUTILITIES DEPOSIT. Any amount Landlord holds and separately identifies as a utilities deposit is handled under Wyo. Stat. § 1-21-1208(b) and not under the paragraphs above.\n\n_______________________    _______________________\nLandlord                   Tenant",
