      "[Optional. Use only if the Premises are within one thousand (1,000) feet of the property on which a school is located, or within one thousand (1,000) feet of the property where a child care facility is located as Wyo. Stat. § 6-2-320(e)(iii) defines that term. Confirm the distance before using this clause and keep the record.]\n\nLocation. Landlord states that the Premises are located within one thousand (1,000) feet of [identify the school or the child care facility], measured from the nearest point on the exterior wall of the Premises to that property's property line.\n\nTenant's obligation. Tenant will not occupy the Premises, and will not permit any other person to occupy the Premises, if that person is eighteen (18) years of age or older and is required to register as a sex offender under Wyo. Stat. § 7-19-302, unless the person is within an exception stated in Wyo. Stat. § 6-2-320(a)(iv) or (a)(v) and has given Landlord written evidence of it before occupying.\n\nVerification. Before any person described above occupies the Premises, Tenant will obtain, or have that person obtain, the determination that Wyo. Stat. § 7-19-302(w) allows an offender to request from the sheriff or the division as to whether the address is within one thousand (1,000) feet of a child care facility, and will give Landlord a copy. Tenant acknowledges that only the offender may make that request, so Landlord relies on Tenant to obtain it.\n\nOngoing duty. Tenant will tell Landlord in writing within five (5) days if any occupant becomes required to register under Wyo. Stat. § 7-19-302 during the tenancy.\n\nBreach. This section is a lawful requirement of this Lease under Wyo. Stat. § 1-21-1204(a)(vii), and a breach is a material breach for which Landlord may terminate and bring an action for forcible entry and detainer under Wyo. Stat. § 1-21-1002(a)(vi), after serving the three (3) day written notice to quit required by Wyo. Stat. § 1-21-1003. Landlord will apply this section to every household on the same terms.",
